======================================================================================================================
  THE DYNAMICS.  A daughter is a Newtonian particle in the expanding background (the kernel-invisible pair): its peculiar
  speed decays as 1/a and its comoving reach saturates at ~0.72-0.79 v_inf/H0 = 6.2-7.6 Mpc whatever its birth epoch.
  That is larger than any galaxy's or group's Lagrangian radius and well inside any X-COP cluster's (A1).  FK1's trigger sends out
  the cosmic share (~0.45) of every host's carrier (A2), so what a host keeps is what it recaptures.
  WHERE THEY GO.  Galaxies do not get them back: the flagship hosts hold <= 0.002 of their own escaped daughters
  inside r200, and escaped daughters refill r_F to <= 0.0035 of the NFW carrier (R2).  Clusters do: hosts >= 4e14 hold
  0.52-0.58 of their own inside r200 by z = 0 (R1).  At z = 2.5 almost every escaped daughter is in the field (R3).
  THE VALIDATION.  The same shell model with the PM's own trigger over-predicts the committed PM's retention: by
  +0.07 to +0.11 at its most massive halos (V1's 0.10 fell at 600) and up to +0.40 at 6e13-2.5e14 (V2).
  PARTIAL.  The bias strengthens the cluster failures; the PM-calibrated reading removes it, and the PM's own most massive
  halos already keep 0.79-0.85 > 0.769 (V4): X-COP's failure does not rest on the model.
  THE GATES.  Flagship (max 0.0439 dex), z = 0 galaxies, KiDS, S_8: pass.  X-COP: FAIL at every kick, both footings, raw
  and calibrated (eps(R500) 0.91-0.93 against <= 0.669).
  Cosmic shear (1.75 Mpc): FAIL in the raw model, reading-dependent once calibrated.  Harvey: 575 FAIL, 650 FAIL
  (hollow cores: the recaptured daughters load the outskirts).  Forest: not established.
  THE WEB (XR19).  With the carrier the halos did not convert converted in the web (nominal, most conservative, turned-
  around shells), X-COP still fails the strict window (eps(R500) 0.82-0.92 raw, 0.74-0.80 calibrated): the web
  daughters are born in the cluster's own infall region, Hubble-cooled and bound (0.21-0.27 of the proto-cluster's
  own web daughters inside R500).  Only the turned-around-web + calibration corner enters L354's NON-THERMAL window
  (575, 600, 625, 650 km/s); Harvey fails there in the halo-only profiles (unscored with the web).
  THE WINDOW.  EMPTY on FP10's strict X-COP criterion in every reading (halo-only raw and calibrated; the three web
  brackets): FP10's optimistic 3/6 cells assumed daughters that never return; the dynamics returns them to the clusters,
  which is FP10's IN-PLACE verdict for X-COP (and, raw, for shear).  One splitting cannot clear galaxies and clusters with the
  same kick -- X-COP alone would need v_k ~1047 km/s (G10), L372's single-channel pincer again.
  NOT settled here: 3-D structure, the web's own conversion (XR19), the forest.  Not 'closed' as a theory.

